# Agent prompt authoring

Studio prompts are pasted standalone. Keep them lean:

- Who the agent is and what it owns
- What to read first (workspace files from the catalog)
- What it must not do (other agents' jobs)
- Pointer to attached skills by name — tools, demo inventory, and schemas
  stay in the skill. Do not paste a skip/implicate decision tree into the
  prompt either.

Do not paste another agent's workflow. Do not paste MCP argument schemas.
Do not paste the four-act demo essay. Cursor's map is `docs/system.md` and
`agents/README.md` packets; Studio agents never see those files.

Default deployed model is **MiniMax**. Author so MiniMax can follow the
prompt without Sonnet. Sonnet is an exception — see `.cursor/rules/minimax-first.mdc`.

Reply contract: `agents/REPLY-CONTRACT.md` — inline the block, do not invent a
new shape.

When reads/writes change, update `skills/workspace-handoff` catalog in the same
change. Name only those paths in the prompt. Do not add scratch workspace
files. Every workspace writer inlines the fleet FS contract: built-in
`read_file`/`write_file` are workspace-relative; never
`Internal directory`, `/shared_workspace/` (including a UUID
`HAI-ASSISTANTS-WAPSPACES` path), or `sessions/`. MiniMax Lifecycle:
if Access denied lists `file_explorer`, retry
`file_explorer/<catalog row>` — that is the catalog, not a new
tree. Health Monitor: one telemetry source per invoke; live ids in
`health/metadata-splunk.json` / `health/metadata-thousandeyes.json`,
not the prompt. See `.cursor/rules/health-visits.mdc`
and `.cursor/rules/catalog-writes-only.mdc`.

**Prompt version.** Every pasteable `agents/*-agent.md` has YAML frontmatter
`version:` and a matching `Version x.y.z.` line under the H1. Bump both in
the same edit. Record the number in `agents/VERSIONS.md`. Do not paste the
frontmatter into Studio.
